(window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS=window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS||{})["troubleshooting"]="<header class=\"mc-head\"><p class=\"mc-eyebrow\">Help<\/p><h2 class=\"mc-title\" tabindex=\"-1\">Messages and troubleshooting<\/h2><p class=\"mc-lede\">What every notice and warning means, and what to do about it.<\/p><p class=\"applies\" data-applies=\"both\">Applies to <b>MODERN and CLASSIC<\/b><\/p><\/header><p>This chapter lists every message XZ Mods can show you, what it means and the one thing to do about it. Find the words you see on the screen in the tables below. Messages in capitals come from the player. Messages in normal case come from the XZ Mods app on your computer.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-if-the-player-will-not-start-with-the-usb\" data-anchor=\"if-the-player-will-not-start-with-the-usb\">If the player will not start with the USB<\/h3>\n<p>XZ Mods never changes the player's firmware, so the player always starts stock without the USB.<\/p>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Switch the player off.<\/li><li>Remove the XZ Mods USB and switch the player on. It starts stock. Play from a stick without XZ Mods if you are in a set.<\/li><li>On your computer, open the USB in the XZ Mods app. If it says <strong>Update available<\/strong>, choose <strong>Update USB<\/strong>. If it says <strong>Up to date<\/strong>, open <strong>Tools<\/strong> › <strong>XZ Mods version<\/strong> › <strong>Restore or update a loader by hand<\/strong> and update the loader again. The app keeps a backup of the old loader each time.<\/li><li>Try the USB again. If it still does not start, <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"troubleshooting\" data-anchor=\"report-a-problem\">report the problem<\/a>.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>Check these first:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Check<\/th><th>Why<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>The player runs firmware 1.26<\/td><td>XZ Mods supports no other firmware version<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>autoexec.bin<\/code> is at the top of the USB<\/td><td>A loader prepared into a folder has to be copied to the USB yourself<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>You updated the USB after updating the app<\/td><td>An app update does not change the USB<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>If XZ Mods started after a network update and stopped working, open <strong>CONNECT<\/strong> › <strong>UPDATES<\/strong> and push <strong>PREVIOUS VERSION<\/strong>, then switch the player off and on. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"connect\" data-anchor=\"updates-over-the-network\">Updates over the network<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>If the sound goes wrong while you test, stop playback and switch the player off and on. Load the same track again and check the original mix before you go on.<\/p>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--tip\"><b>Tip<\/b><p>MODS is always reachable with the hardware alone. In CLASSIC, the rekordbox button above LINK switches to MODERN, where <kbd>MENU<\/kbd> opens MODS. Turn the encoder to move, push it to choose and press <kbd>BACK<\/kbd> to go back.<\/p><\/aside>\n<h3 id=\"m-stems-on-the-usb\" data-anchor=\"stems-on-the-usb\">Stems on the USB<\/h3>\n<p>When a deck cannot play stems, its stem row says why and its last button offers the next step. In CLASSIC the row sits under the deck's waveform. Open the button to see the deck's setup page in MODS.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-1\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · USB STEMS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b958d49795785217.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Deck 1 has a track loaded that has no stems yet.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"46.500\" data-y=\"12.292\" aria-label=\"1: STANDALONE STEMS SETUP\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-1-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"60.750\" data-y=\"17.083\" aria-label=\"2: Steps\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-1-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"42.000\" data-y=\"28.958\" aria-label=\"3: Deck state\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-1-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"62.500\" data-y=\"38.542\" aria-label=\"4: Next step\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-1-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"63.375\" data-y=\"4.167\" aria-label=\"5: Deck\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-1-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"46.500\" data-y=\"74.167\" aria-label=\"6: CHECK THIS DECK AGAIN\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-1-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"82.000\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"7: State\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-1-7\">7<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Deck 1 has a track loaded that has no stems yet.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-1-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>STANDALONE STEMS SETUP<\/b> <span>The three things stems need, in order.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-1-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Steps<\/b> <span>1 CHECK ENGINE, 2 TURN ON (ALL DECKS), 3 LOAD A PREPARED TRACK.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-1-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Deck state<\/b> <span>The deck and why it has no stems.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-1-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Next step<\/b> <span>The one thing to do.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-1-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Deck<\/b> <span>Choose DECK 1 or DECK 2 to check the other deck.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-1-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>CHECK THIS DECK AGAIN<\/b> <span>Reads the deck again after you fixed it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-1-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>State<\/b> <span>The deck's stem state in a word or two.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stem row says<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><th>What to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>STEMS READY<\/td><td>Stems are ready on this deck<\/td><td>Nothing<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NO STEM ENGINE, with <strong>SET UP<\/strong><\/td><td>The loader on the USB has no stem engine<\/td><td>Update the USB loader with the XZ Mods app, then restart the player<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STEMS OFF, with <strong>TURN ON<\/strong><\/td><td>USB stems are switched off<\/td><td>Push <strong>TURN ON<\/strong>. It turns USB stems on for decks 1 and 2<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NO TRACK LOADED<\/td><td>The deck has no track<\/td><td>Load a track from the USB<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NOT PREPARED, with <strong>HOW TO FIX<\/strong><\/td><td>The track has no stems on this USB<\/td><td>Prepare it in the XZ Mods app, then load it again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>LOADING STEMS<\/td><td>Stems are loading from the USB<\/td><td>Wait a moment<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>PLAY TO ALIGN<\/td><td>Stems are loaded but not locked to the track yet<\/td><td>Press play. Stems lock to the track a few seconds in<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STEM SET ERROR, with <strong>HOW TO FIX<\/strong><\/td><td>The stems on the USB are incomplete or damaged. The page names the problem<\/td><td>Verify the track in the XZ Mods app and prepare it again<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>Every state on both interfaces, with pictures, is in <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-notices-on-the-play-screen\" data-anchor=\"notices-on-the-play-screen\" data-iface=\"modern\">Notices on the play screen <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>A notice is a short message in the middle of the lanes. It clears on its own after a few seconds, and the deck keeps playing.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-2\" data-iface=\"modern\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODERN · Play screen<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/0b2dd61190edad2d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"A notice over the lanes.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"70.000\" data-y=\"48.125\" aria-label=\"1: Notice\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-2-1\">1<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>A notice over the lanes.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-2-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Notice<\/b> <span>What happened. Nothing else on the screen changes.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-3\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/70bbc985a0f785ef.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A long notice wraps onto two lines\"><img src=\"manual/shots/70bbc985a0f785ef.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A long notice wraps onto two lines<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Notice<\/th><th>What to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>DECK 1 DID NOT LOAD THE TRACK<\/td><td>Load the track again. If it fails again, check the file in rekordbox<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>THE TRACK ON USB 2 COULD NOT BE READ BECAUSE THE DEVICE WAS REMOVED WHILE IT WAS LOADING<\/td><td>Plug the USB back in and load the track again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>USB1 IS NOT CONNECTED, USB2 IS NOT CONNECTED<\/td><td>Plug in the USB, or choose the other source<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>USB SOURCE CHANGED: SELECT TRACK AGAIN<\/td><td>The USB changed under the list. Choose the track again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SELECT A TRACK, THEN PRESS LOAD<\/td><td>Highlight a track first<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>OPEN A TRACK LIST TO LOAD, NO USB TRACK LIST TO LOAD FROM<\/td><td>Open a track list on a USB, then load<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>LOAD FROM THIS LIST IS OFF<\/td><td>Loading from this list is switched off. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"browse\">Browsing and loading<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>THIS ROW CANNOT BE LOADED, THAT DECK CANNOT LOAD THIS TRACK<\/td><td>Choose another track or another deck<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TAG LIST IS FULL: 100 TRACKS<\/td><td>Remove a track from the tag list first<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>MATCHING NEEDS A MASTER DECK<\/td><td>Set a master deck, then use MATCHING<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NO MASTER DECK: BPM FILTER OFF, NO MASTER KEY: KEY FILTER OFF<\/td><td>The filter has nothing to compare with. Set a master deck<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>COMPUTER BROWSING IS NOT AVAILABLE YET, LINK BROWSING IS NOT AVAILABLE YET<\/td><td>Browse a USB instead. These sources come in a later version<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>LINK DID NOT OPEN, EXPORT MODE DID NOT OPEN<\/td><td>Try again. The player's own screen did not open<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>MODS DID NOT OPEN: PUSH AGAIN<\/td><td>Push again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TOUCH CANNOT OPEN THIS YET: PUSH THE ENCODER<\/td><td>Use the encoder for this item<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>THAT SETTING CANNOT CHANGE HERE<\/td><td>Change it in the player's own UTILITY. Hold <kbd>MENU<\/kbd><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>DECK 3 AND 4 ARE NOT RUNNING<\/td><td>Set up four decks first. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>KEY SHIFT REFUSED: AUDIO LOAD TOO HIGH<\/td><td>The measured audio workload leaves too little headroom for a new shift. Current shifts keep running. Check SYSTEM READOUT and retry when the load falls. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"keys-and-key-sync\">Keys and KEY SYNC<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>THIS DECK IS MASTER<\/td><td>KEY SYNC matches a deck to the master. Make another deck the master first<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A player warning such as E-8307: USB ACCESS ERROR<\/td><td>The player raised its own warning window. MODERN says it once in the player's words and keeps working. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"troubleshooting\" data-anchor=\"the-player-s-own-warnings\">The player's own warnings<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>THIS DJ PROFILE CANNOT BE READ<\/td><td>Make the profile again in the XZ Mods app. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"connect\" data-anchor=\"when-a-profile-will-not-save-or-show\">Connect and DJ profiles<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-errors-on-a-deck\" data-anchor=\"errors-on-a-deck\">Errors on a deck<\/h3>\n<p>When the player cannot play a track, XZ Mods shows the player's own error code and text on that deck. XZ Mods never hides these errors.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-4\" data-iface=\"modern\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODERN · Play screen<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c6266a54d7583b0b.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"A read error on deck 2.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"50.000\" data-y=\"43.333\" aria-label=\"1: Error\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-4-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"78.750\" data-y=\"44.583\" aria-label=\"2: CHOOSE TRACK\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-4-2\">2<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>A read error on deck 2.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-4-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Error<\/b> <span>The player's own code and text.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-4-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>CHOOSE TRACK<\/b> <span>Opens browse so you can load another track.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-5\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/709966e3cc33a46d.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: EMERGENCY LOOP. The deck loops until you load a track\"><img src=\"manual/shots/709966e3cc33a46d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>EMERGENCY LOOP. The deck loops until you load a track<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/71e1c434ffa9e422.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The same error on deck 3, with four decks\"><img src=\"manual/shots/71e1c434ffa9e422.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The same error on deck 3, with four decks<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<ul><li><strong>MODERN.<\/strong> The error covers the deck's lane, with <strong>CHOOSE TRACK<\/strong>. While MODS is open, the strip at the top of the dock turns red with each deck's badge, the code, the player's text and <strong>SHOW DECK<\/strong>. Tap the strip to close MODS and see the deck.<\/li><li><strong>CLASSIC.<\/strong> The player's own error stays visible in the deck's lower area, also while MODS is open. Touches there go to the player.<\/li><\/ul>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Code<\/th><th>Player's text<\/th><th>What to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>E-8302<\/td><td>CANNOT PLAY TRACK<\/td><td>Load another track. Check the USB and the file on a computer<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>E-8304, E-8305<\/td><td>UNSUPPORTED<\/td><td>The player cannot play this file. Export it in another format<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>E-8306<\/td><td>NO FILE<\/td><td>The file is missing from the USB. Export the track from rekordbox again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>E-7206<\/td><td>AUTH CHIP ERROR<\/td><td>Switch the player off and on. If it also happens without the XZ Mods USB, the player needs service<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-player-s-own-warnings\" data-anchor=\"the-player-s-own-warnings\">The player's own warnings<\/h3>\n<p>The player sometimes raises its own warning window, for example about a USB or a device. A warning never takes the screen or the controls away from XZ Mods.<\/p>\n<ul><li><strong>MODERN.<\/strong> The play screen says the warning once, in the player's own words, for example <strong>E-8307: USB ACCESS ERROR<\/strong>. Browse, the decks and every control keep working.<\/li><li><strong>MODS, in either interface.<\/strong> MODS stays open on the same page. The strip at the top of the dock turns red with the warning's code and text, and <strong>REPORT THIS<\/strong>. The strip goes when the warning does.<\/li><li><strong>CLASSIC with MODS closed.<\/strong> The player's window shows as on a stock XDJ-XZ. Touches, keys and the encoder go to the player until it closes the window.<\/li><\/ul>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-6\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · dock<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/73a673c2bb15580a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"A player warning in the dock while MODS is open.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/2541b4b35bce5aed.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"A player warning in the dock while MODS is open.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"5.000\" data-y=\"93.125\" aria-label=\"1: Warning\" aria-describedby=\"f-troubleshooting-6-1\">1<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>A player warning in the dock while MODS is open.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-troubleshooting-6-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Warning<\/b> <span>The player's code and text.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<h4 id=\"m-e-8307-hubs-are-not-supported\" data-anchor=\"e-8307-hubs-are-not-supported\">E-8307: HUBS ARE NOT SUPPORTED<\/h4>\n<p>The player sees the loopback cable for four decks as a hub. It raises <strong>E-8307: HUBS ARE NOT SUPPORTED<\/strong> or <strong>E-8307: UNSUPPORTED DEVICE<\/strong> and keeps it up while the cable is in. It is not an error, so XZ Mods never shows it: MODERN and MODS show nothing, and in CLASSIC the player's window turns into a calm <strong>LOOPBACK CABLE CONNECTED<\/strong> card. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\" data-anchor=\"the-e-8307-hub-warning\">Four decks<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-when-settings-cannot-be-saved\" data-anchor=\"when-settings-cannot-be-saved\">When settings cannot be saved<\/h3>\n<p>Every change in MODS saves on its own to the USB. The save state at the right of the MODS dock says what happened. Lines that say NOT SAVED or NO SETTINGS USB show in amber. The full list is in <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"mods-menu\" data-anchor=\"saving-to-the-usb\">Saving to the USB<\/a>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Message<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><th>What to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>NO SETTINGS USB: CHANGES LAST UNTIL POWER OFF.<\/td><td>No USB to save on<\/td><td>Insert the XZ Mods USB, or your settings USB<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NOT SAVED TO USB 1: CHECK USB<\/td><td>Writing failed<\/td><td>Check the stick is in and not write-protected, then change the setting again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>USB 1 IS LOCKED: NOT SAVED<\/td><td>The stick is write-protected<\/td><td>Unlock it, or check it on a computer<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>THE STICK IS FULL: NOT SAVED<\/td><td>No space left on the stick<\/td><td>Free some space on a computer<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>THIS STICK IS READ-ONLY: NOTHING CHANGES<\/td><td>The player opened the stick read-only<\/td><td>Check the stick on a computer<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>INVALID USB SETTINGS: KEPT CURRENT, USB 1 SETTINGS INVALID: KEPT CURRENT<\/td><td>The settings file on the stick is damaged. The player keeps the settings it has<\/td><td>Change any setting to write a new file, or update the USB in the app<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>USB 1 HAS NO SETTINGS: KEPT CURRENT<\/td><td>The stick has no settings yet<\/td><td>Nothing. Your next change creates them<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>PROFILE APPLIED / NOT SAVED<\/td><td>A DJ profile was applied but could not be saved<\/td><td>Check the stick is in and not locked<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SETTINGS SAVE UNAVAILABLE<\/td><td>Saving stopped in this session<\/td><td>Switch the player off and on<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NOT SAVED: CHANGES LAST UNTIL POWER OFF., TRIAL RUN: NOTHING SAVED<\/td><td>This build runs as a trial that saves nothing<\/td><td>Start from a USB prepared in the XZ Mods app to save<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TRIAL RUN: SETTINGS NOT LOADED<\/td><td>A trial build ignores the settings on the stick<\/td><td>Start from a prepared USB<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>A padlock beside a setting means XZ Mods shows it but cannot change it there. The help under it says why. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"mods-menu\" data-anchor=\"utility-the-player-s-own-settings\">UTILITY, the player's own settings<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-messages-in-the-xz-mods-app\" data-anchor=\"messages-in-the-xz-mods-app\">Messages in the XZ Mods app<\/h3>\n<p>Every \"needs setup\" state in the app comes with one button that starts a short guide. Press it.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Message<\/th><th>Button<\/th><th>What it does<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>No XZ Mods build is on this computer yet, so there is nothing to write<\/td><td><strong>Set up mod versions<\/strong><\/td><td>Finds or imports a build<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Choose which XZ Mods build goes on this USB<\/td><td><strong>Use the newest build<\/strong><\/td><td>Picks the build that came with the app<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Stem engine not set up yet<\/td><td><strong>Set up stem engine<\/strong><\/td><td>Checks the computer, downloads the engine and tests it<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Connect a Rekordbox USB<\/td><td><strong>Connect a USB<\/strong><\/td><td>Finds a USB or a folder and checks its library<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Set up Live Streamer to connect to your XZ<\/td><td><strong>Set up Live Streamer<\/strong><\/td><td>Finds the XZ on the network and connects<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Older USB loaders have no screen service<\/td><td><strong>Update the USB loader<\/strong><\/td><td>Opens the USB page to update the loader<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Rekordbox is open on this computer<\/td><td><strong>Prepare for repair<\/strong><\/td><td>Waits for you to close rekordbox, then checks again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Not confirmed yet, after sending a report<\/td><td><strong>Set up reporting connection<\/strong><\/td><td>Checks the internet connection and the clock, then sends the same report again. It never arrives twice<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Maintainer inbox, not connected (maintainer only)<\/td><td><strong>Connect and check<\/strong><\/td><td>Keeps the owner key under Windows protection and reads the inbox to check it<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Message<\/th><th>What to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USB drives could not be listed<\/td><td>Choose <strong>Choose a folder instead<\/strong>, or plug the USB in again and choose <strong>Look again<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The USB could not be read<\/td><td>Reconnect it and choose it again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>This is a folder, not a USB<\/td><td>Copy the finished <code>autoexec.bin<\/code> to the top of the USB afterward<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Nothing to write yet<\/td><td>Add a game or a DJ profile, or cancel<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>XZ Mods is updating itself<\/td><td>Write to the USB once the app update has finished<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Finished, with something to check<\/td><td>Read the lines under it. <strong>Retry the failed games<\/strong> tries only the games that failed<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Settings were not written<\/td><td>Open the USB again and write again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Your DJ profile was not saved<\/td><td>Read the reason under it, fix it and save the profile again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The USB was not ejected<\/td><td>Choose <strong>Try ejecting again<\/strong>, or eject it from your computer<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Making stems needs a Windows computer or an Apple silicon Mac<\/td><td>Import stems made elsewhere, or make them on another computer<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The graphics engine needs a newer NVIDIA driver<\/td><td>Choose <strong>Use the processor<\/strong>, or update the driver and check again<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The USB is full<\/td><td>Choose <strong>Choose fewer tracks<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The USB was disconnected<\/td><td>Plug it back in and choose <strong>Continue<\/strong>. Nothing was left half-written<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>Every page of the app is in <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"desktop-app\">The XZ Mods app<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-diary-on-your-usb-sticks\" data-anchor=\"the-diary-on-your-usb-sticks\">The diary on your USB sticks<\/h3>\n<p>XZ Mods keeps a short diagnostic diary in <code>VJ.Tools/XZ-Mods-diary/<\/code> on each mounted USB stick, including music sticks. If a problem happens during a set, keep those sticks so you can include their diaries in a later report.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mx\" data-mx=\"usb-diary\" data-mode=\"scenes\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"How the diary fills a stick\"><ol class=\"mx-scenes\"><li data-title=\"Writing\"><b>Writing<\/b> <span>XZ Mods writes a short diagnostic diary in VJ.Tools/XZ-Mods-diary on each mounted USB stick.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"Full\"><b>Full<\/b> <span>Each stick holds at most 4 MiB of diary files. Older segments are replaced first.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"Pauses\"><b>Pauses<\/b> <span>Writing pauses during track loads, RAM copies and heavy USB reads.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"Never recorded\"><b>Never recorded<\/b> <span>The diary never records track titles, music paths, serial numbers or network identities.<\/span><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<p>The diary records the XZ Mods version, settings fingerprint, USB slots, interface, deck view, state changes and fixed notice codes. It also records available CPU, memory, audio, SYNC, key-processing and USB-read measurements. It never records track titles, music paths, serial numbers or network identities. A missing measurement stays unknown.<\/p>\n<p>Each stick holds at most 4 MiB of diary files. Older segments are replaced first, and the previous session's latest segment is kept when a new session starts. Writing pauses during track loads, RAM copies and heavy USB reads. No diary is created on a read-only stick or when less than 64 MiB of free space plus a small write reserve remains. Read-only test sessions save nothing. Normal USB-loader sessions write diary entries when these conditions allow it. Long busy periods and removal can leave gaps.<\/p>\n<p>The diary stays on the sticks. Nothing is sent until you choose to include it in a report.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-report-a-problem\" data-anchor=\"report-a-problem\">Report a problem<\/h3>\n<p>When something goes wrong, send a report. It helps fix the problem for everyone.<\/p>\n<ul><li><strong>On the player.<\/strong> Open MODS › <strong>EXTRAS<\/strong> › <strong>REPORT AN ISSUE<\/strong>, or push <strong>REPORT THIS<\/strong> beside an error in the dock. Choose a topic, add words if you like, and send. Offline, the report waits on the stick for your computer. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"extras\" data-anchor=\"report-an-issue\">Report an issue<\/a>.<\/li><li><strong>On your computer.<\/strong> In the XZ Mods app, open <strong>Feedback<\/strong> at the foot of the rail and choose <strong>Report a problem<\/strong>. Only one box is required, and <strong>My reports<\/strong> in Feedback shows where your report is afterwards. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"desktop-app\" data-anchor=\"report-a-problem-or-share-an-idea\">Report a problem or share an idea<\/a>.<\/li><li><strong>On GitHub.<\/strong> Open an issue at https://github.com/OpticMystic/XZ-Mods/issues.<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>Say what you did, what you expected and what happened. The app adds the cleaned-up details itself, and you can see and untick each one. Nothing is sent until you press <strong>Send privately<\/strong>, and the app posts nothing publicly. From the player, the public GitHub issue is a separate step you submit yourself.<\/p>";
